    "body": "## Problem\n\n`BindNamedParameters` rejects unknown named parameters even when the function has `varargs = LogicalType::ANY`. A function that accepts any positional arg should also accept any named param.\n\n## Current behavior\n\n```sql\n-- Function registered with varargs = ANY, no named_parameters declared\nSELECT * FROM my_func('file.csv', header:=true);\n-- Error: Invalid named parameter \"header\"\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nWhen `varargs = ANY`, pass all named parameters through to the bind function without validation.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n`src/planner/binder/tableref/bind_named_parameters.cpp`, line 14:\n\n```diff\n  if (entry == types.end()) {\n+   // varargs=ANY functions accept any named parameter\n+   if (types.empty()) continue;\n    // ... existing error ...\n  }\n```\n\n## Context\n\nNeeded for [Airport extension passthrough mode](https://github.com/Query-farm/airport/pull/49) — forwarding arbitrary SQL (including `read_csv` with named params) to a remote DuckDB.",
